00:55:01,313 --> 00:55:04,380
Speaker 1: You are not machines, you are not cattle, you are men.

644
00:55:05,060 --> 00:55:06,866
Speaker 2: You have the love of humanity in your hearts.

645
00:55:07,227 --> 00:55:08,973
Speaker 2: You don't hate, only the unloved.

646
00:55:09,013 --> 00:55:11,020
Speaker 2: hate, the unloved and the unnatural.

647
00:55:11,560 --> 00:55:14,546
Speaker 2: Soldiers, don't fight for slavery, fight for liberty.

648
00:55:14,927 --> 00:55:16,129
Speaker 2: In the seventeenth chapter of St.

649
00:55:16,149 --> 00:55:16,289
Speaker 2: Luke.

650
00:55:16,309 --> 00:55:21,780
Speaker 0: it is written, the kingdom of God is within man, not one man nor a group of men, but in all men, in you.

651
00:55:22,181 --> 00:55:26,909
Speaker 1: You the people have the power, the power to create machines, the power to create happiness.

652
00:55:27,150 --> 00:55:32,500
Speaker 1: You the people have the power to make this life free and beautiful, to make this life a wonderful adventure.

653
00:55:32,960 --> 00:55:45,180
Speaker 1: Then in the name of democracy, let us use that power, let us all unite, let us fight for a new world, a decent world that will give men a chance to work, that will give youth a future and old age a security.

654
00:55:45,641 --> 00:55:55,520
Speaker 2: By the promise of these things, brutes have risen to power, but they lie, they do not fulfill that promise, they never will, dictators free themselves, but they enslave the people.

655
00:55:56,060 --> 00:56:06,180
Speaker 2: Now let us fight to fulfill that promise, let us fight to free the world, to do away with national barriers, to do away with greed, with hate and intolerance.

656
00:56:06,920 --> 00:56:12,880
Speaker 1: Let us fight for a world of reason, a world where science and progress will lead to all men's happiness.

657
00:56:13,744 --> 00:56:17,200
Speaker 2: Soldiers in the name of democracy, let us all unite!

